    "final_answer": "I successfully found the information through the Wayback Machine archive. Let me record the key findings:\n\n**British Pronunciation (UK):** /juːˈfɔː.ri.ə/\n\n**Example sentences from Cambridge Dictionary:**\n1. \"They were in a state of euphoria for days after they won the prize.\"\n2. \"The drug produces a feeling of euphoria.\"\n3. \"After the initial euphoria at getting the contract wore off, we realized how much work we had to do.\"\n4. \"Euphoria turned to dismay when colleagues began to suspect his experimental results were faked.\"\n5. \"The victorious team returned to a wave of national euphoria.\"\n\n---\n\n## Final Answer\n\nI was able to complete the task using the Wayback Machine archive of the Cambridge Dictionary, since the live site was blocking automated access with a Cloudflare security verification challenge.\n\n**British Pronunciation of \"euphoria\":**\n**/juːˈfɔː.ri.ə/** (British English)\n\n**Example sentence from Cambridge Dictionary:**\n*\"They were in a state of euphoria for days after they won the prize.\"*\n\nAdditional example sentences also shown on the page:\n- \"The drug produces a feeling of euphoria.\"\n- \"After the initial euphoria at getting the contract wore off, we realized how much work we had to do.\"\n- \"Euphoria turned to dismay when colleagues began to suspect his experimental results were faked.\"\n- \"The victorious team returned to a wave of national euphoria.\"\n\n**Definition (from Cambridge Dictionary):** *extreme happiness, sometimes more than is reasonable in a particular situation*\n\nNote: The live Cambridge Dictionary site (dictionary.cambridge.org) was returning a Cloudflare \"verify you are human\" security challenge that the automated browser could not pass. I successfully retrieved the same content via archive.org's Wayback Machine snapshot of the Cambridge Dictionary page for \"euphoria\" (captured July 6, 2024).",
